{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  input %x: uint\n  output %out: uint (stored to; its values are listed after the run)\nsimplify: 15 SPIR-V instructions, 0 rewrites proved by SAT (bit-precise: equal for every input), 1 division by a constant made a multiply and a shift (derived, below), 0 dead instructions removed\n  assuming x in [0, 255] (every load of it)\n  integer arithmetic cost under gt1030 (each instruction once): 13.5 -> 9 (-33.3%)\n  by kind:\n       1  a division by a constant of a bounded dividend as a multiply and a shift  -4.5\n  rewrites:\n    %r = OpUMod %uint %x %uint_3\n      ->  %x - 3(171%x >> 9)   (a division by a constant of a bounded dividend as a multiply and a shift; -4.5)\n  divisions by a constant (the dividend's bound makes one multiply and one shift exact; derived by idrw.c, kept under gt1030):\n    %r = OpUMod %uint %x %uint_3\n      ->  %x - 3(171%x >> 9)   (cost 13.5 -> 9)\n      holds where %x in [0, 255] (its range)\n      M = ceil(2^9/3) = 171, so M*3 = 2^9 + 1\n      x*M/2^9 = x/3 + x*1/(3*2^9): the excess is below 1/3 while x*1 < 2^9, and x/3 is at least 1/3 below the next integer, so floor(x*M/2^9) = floor(x/3)\n      x <= 255: x*1 <= 255 < 2^9, and x*M <= 43605 < 2^32, so the product does not wrap in u32\n      and x % 3 = x - 3*floor(x/3)\n  range search on a result (one input, x in [0, 255]; every one of the 256 inputs checked):\n    nothing cheaper than its cost 9 among 1970144 forms of (x + K) >> S, (x +- (x >> S1) + K) >> S and t = x + K; (t +- (t >> S1)) >> S\n  proved; the operands' definitions were expanded up to 16 levels, the rest (loads, loop phis, spec constants) are free inputs\n  (nofile: simplified.spvasm, 642 bytes, checksum fb1b430c)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "spirv_simplify", "ucas": "spvsimplify nofile assume x 0 255", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "spirv_simplify", "instructions": 15, "dead_removed": 0, "model": "gt1030", "cost_before": 13.5, "cost_after": 9, "assumptions": [{"name": "x", "lo": 0, "hi": 255}], "rewrites": [{"from": "%r = OpUMod %uint %x %uint_3", "to": "%x - 3(171%x >> 9)", "why": "a division by a constant of a bounded dividend as a multiply and a shift", "gain": 4.5, "line": 0, "proof": "derivation"}], "identities": [{"from": "%r = OpUMod %uint %x %uint_3", "to": "%x - 3(171%x >> 9)", "line": 0, "cost_before": 13.5, "cost_after": 9, "holds_where": "%x in [0, 255] (its range)", "derivation": "M = ceil(2^9/3) = 171, so M*3 = 2^9 + 1\nx*M/2^9 = x/3 + x*1/(3*2^9): the excess is below 1/3 while x*1 < 2^9, and x/3 is at least 1/3 below the next integer, so floor(x*M/2^9) = floor(x/3)\nx <= 255: x*1 <= 255 < 2^9, and x*M <= 43605 < 2^32, so the product does not wrap in u32\nand x % 3 = x - 3*floor(x/3)"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "derivation", "text": "each rewrite carries its own proof and domain: derived rewrites hold only where their stated assumptions do (see holds_where), the rest bit-blasted and proved equal for every input (refinement)"}, "files": [], "text": "  input %x: uint\n  output %out: uint (stored to; its values are listed after the run)\nsimplify: 15 SPIR-V instructions, 0 rewrites proved by SAT (bit-precise: equal for every input), 1 division by a constant made a multiply and a shift (derived, below), 0 dead instructions removed\n  assuming x in [0, 255] (every load of it)\n  integer arithmetic cost under gt1030 (each instruction once): 13.5 -> 9 (-33.3%)\n  by kind:\n       1  a division by a constant of a bounded dividend as a multiply and a shift  -4.5\n  rewrites:\n    %r = OpUMod %uint %x %uint_3\n      ->  %x - 3(171%x >> 9)   (a division by a constant of a bounded dividend as a multiply and a shift; -4.5)\n  divisions by a constant (the dividend's bound makes one multiply and one shift exact; derived by idrw.c, kept under gt1030):\n    %r = OpUMod %uint %x %uint_3\n      ->  %x - 3(171%x >> 9)   (cost 13.5 -> 9)\n      holds where %x in [0, 255] (its range)\n      M = ceil(2^9/3) = 171, so M*3 = 2^9 + 1\n      x*M/2^9 = x/3 + x*1/(3*2^9): the excess is below 1/3 while x*1 < 2^9, and x/3 is at least 1/3 below the next integer, so floor(x*M/2^9) = floor(x/3)\n      x <= 255: x*1 <= 255 < 2^9, and x*M <= 43605 < 2^32, so the product does not wrap in u32\n      and x % 3 = x - 3*floor(x/3)\n  range search on a result (one input, x in [0, 255]; every one of the 256 inputs checked):\n    nothing cheaper than its cost 9 among 1970144 forms of (x + K) >> S, (x +- (x >> S1) + K) >> S and t = x + K; (t +- (t >> S1)) >> S\n  proved; the operands' definitions were expanded up to 16 levels, the rest (loads, loop phis, spec constants) are free inputs\n  (nofile: simplified.spvasm, 642 bytes, checksum fb1b430c)\n"}, "isError": false}}
